SEC. 51P-251.114. SCREENING.

(a) Screening of a parking lot for a private school from an adjacent public right-of-way must use the following materials:

(1) a three-foot-high solid screening fence;

(2) an earthen berm with a minimum height of three feet planted with turf grass or ground cover;

(3) evergreen plant materials recommended for local use by the building official with a minimum height of three feet at maturity;

(4) a masonry retaining wall topped with solid fencing with a total height of six feet; or

(5) a combination of these materials.

(b) Screening of a parking lot for a private school from an adjacent residential use must use the following materials:

(1) a six-foot-high solid screening fence;

(2) an earthen berm with a minimum height of six feet planted with turf grass or ground cover;

(3) evergreen plant materials recommended for local use by the building official with a minimum height of six feet at maturity;

(4) a masonry retaining wall topped with solid fencing with a total height of six feet; or

(5) a combination of these materials. (Ord. Nos. 25499; 25711; 26576)
